## Summary

✅ **DO:**
- Use Angular Reactive Forms with type safety
- Create custom validators
- Use Signals for real-time calculations
- Centralize form state in services
- Use `class` (not `className`)
- Provide clear validation messages
- Mark forms as touched on submit
- Use component classes (`.input`, `.btn-primary`)

❌ **DON'T:**
- Use React Hook Form or Zod
- Use template-driven forms for complex scenarios
- Skip type safety
- Forget accessibility (labels, ARIA)
- Use inline styles
- Skip error handling
